                <pb facs="1210" n="1116" sameAs="frus:frus1887/pg1116"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1 in No. 25.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">American Bible Society to
                        the President</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Bible House, Astor Place</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">New
                                York</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1887-04-07"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">April</hi> 7,
                    1887</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The board of managers of the American Bible
                    Society, through t Je undersigned, its committee, begs leave to call your
                    attention to the injustice done to its agents and employés in the Turkish Empire
                    while engaged in the sale of Bibles and Testaments whose publication has been
                    approved by the, ministry of public instruction, and of the copies of the Holy
                    Scriptures which have passed through the customhouse, after examination and the
                    payment of duties. Our information is that those agents and employés are
                    constantly and wrongfully interrupted in their lawful work, and are subjected to
                    imprisonment and other indignities. Not only in provinces remote from the
                    capital, but in Constantinople itself, the police in repeated instances have
                    disregarded treaty and law, so that our employés have been arrested and
                    imprisoned, and their books have been seized in an unjust and arbitrary manner.
                    In support of these statements we append a printed but unpublished letter from
                    Dr. Isaac G. Bliss, agent of the Society for the Levant, and we beg leave to ask
                    that instructions may be given, through the State Department, to the United
                    States legation at Constantinople to protest against these interruptions to the
                    society’s lawful work, and, if possible, to prevent their recurrence.</p>
                <p>We are, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><list>
                            <item><hi rendition="#small-caps">Enoch L. Fancher</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                    rendition="#italic">President of American-Bible
                                Society.</hi></item>
                            <item><hi rendition="#small-caps">Edward W. Gilman</hi>,</item>
                            <item><hi rendition="#small-caps">Alexander McLean</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                    rendition="#italic">Corresponding Secretaries.</hi></item>
                        </list></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
